        <p>At a meeting of the Watch Committee of the York Corporation on Wednesday, deputations from the Small Traders' Protection Association and from the citizens who approve of the action of the Corporation in ordering the recent prosecutions for Sunday trading were heard. Mr. Leavis, on behalf of the Small Traders' Association, announced that no matter what the Council might decide, at least 13 Of the small traders would continue to keep open on Sundays regardless of the consequences. After a long dis- cussion it was decided by a majority of the Watch Committee to recommend the Council to adopt the following arrangement as a way out of the difficulty : Provision dealers' shops to be open until 1 p.m. and from 5 to 6 p.m; shops selling tobacco,sweetsAc., from 1 p.m. to 10 p.m.</p>
