      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-07-26_WidnesExaminer_art0173" n="art0173">
        <head>JOTTINGS BY AN OLD</head>
        <p>JOTTINGS BY AN OLD</p>
        <p>JOURNALIST.</p>
        <p>]:l4-9RE ABOUT PICKPOCKETS. ihe conviction of London pickpockets on :Agecount of operations in the crowds on the ,t'aY of the Royal visit to Warrington f 'oeininded me of the summary methods •e,, the police on such occasions half a ;antury ago. lt is just over fifty years :pgr? since the late King Edward, as elee of Wales, opened the Halifax Town a:P. There were great doings, of course, ' the elaborate decorations and illumina- reuns attracted immense multitudes. As I i tllrkcd in my last, and as was proved n cas the eat Warrington, this sort of thing is of-i- at opportunity, and a precious gang a kton 'ion experts took the 200-mile journey ehfax, in sure and certain hope of a a rtellB harvest. But for once in while they reckoned without their - Nen for on alighting at their destin a- PlatrieY found awaiting them on the station to OUi a number of experienced detectives, thein they were personally known. These 37 conducted them across the line, and ex 4 them off back by the next London liaPvress• I was in Halifax at the time, and aeh.e always admired the smartness of the •st levement. I do not profess to under- booal how the thing was managed within the ithafrids of strict legality, though perhaps 'the— Was not so precisely insisted upon in I.e„,,hlid-Victorian era. Anyhow, the pro- e "lona' thieves seemed only too glad to '.asneda'Pe the detectives' clutches on those terms; sarelY it was better, ever so much better, even letting them loose upon holiday-makers, ba for a few hours. I'uWARE." At s cunt tieh seasons it is and always has been t, 0 ,t 0 InarY for well-meaning local authorities wavoBt conspicuously in public places the " Beware of pickpockets" ; but it is (10,7003b1e whether the harm thereby done It hot more than counterbalance the good. •,per:B natural enough for a thoughtless to Oflsuddenly confronted by such a notice 'lviii"„i.teD and put his hand to the pocket in ,th,Z", he carries his purse to assure himself ke-e,' his cash is safe. Observa