        <head>ODDFELLOWS' MAIN.</head>
        <p>ODDFELLOWS' MAIN.</p>
        <p>The 1.0.0. F., Manchester Unity, Friendly Society (Warrington District).</p>
        <p>The above main, in which the "Sir Gilbert Greenalr Challenge Cup bas to be competed for, will commence at 2 o'clock this afternoon on the Bowling Green Hotel green, Liverpool-road. The handicapping and drawing took place at the hotel on Wednesday eveuiug last. Competitors will be allowed to use their own bowls. Games 13 up. Referee, Mr. William Butter- worth ; measurers, Messrs. Albert E. Burdett and Henry Jones ; hon. secretary, Mr. William E. Clare, 50, Hood- lane. The draw and handicap of the 88 entries is as follows :</p>
        <p>PRELIMINARY ROUND. Alfred Gleave, 2 v J. H. Shelton, 4 I lenry Taylor, 3 v Henry Bradburn, 4 James Leah, 2 v Thomas Watson, 4 Herbert Glover, 2 v C. Crosq, 3 T Broadhurst, 3 v Harry Rowe. 4 John Sankey, 6 v Arthur Foster, 4 M Wilcock, 3 v Charles Whittaker, 4 Fred Miller, 1 v H H Halford, sell., 2 M Finch, 2 v S 11 Dale, 3 James A Melbourne, 1 v Leonard Simpson, 4 William J Hopkins, 3 v Walter Daniels, 4 H Broadhura, 3 v George Bottomley, 3 J Lister, 3 v Edward Bailey, 3 George Higlaam, 6 v Frank Webster, 5. W Bolt, 4 v J T Ellison, 2 Fred Bradburn, 4 v Joseph Booth, 4 Walter Dennett, 4 v Albert E Burdett, 2 .1 Parsons, 1 v Arthur Clare, 3 William Webb, 3 v John T Perry, 3 Peter E Croft, 2 v T Bolton, scr. J W Rigby, 2 v H Stringer, 5 William Paskin, 5 v T J Hopkins, 3 A Perry, 3 v Herbert Wlaitelegg, 6 John Ilankinson, 5 v Israel Dutton, 3 Byes :-Arthur Lawton 2, William Roughley scr, Thomas S. Steel 3, T. Champion 2, John Broadhurst 3, Thomas J. Rigby 3, Fred Owen 1, Fred Howard 3, George Savage 3, Thomas Leather 3, Elijah Lunt 3, N. J. Clarke 3, William Monks 3, Henry Jones 4, Henry Lawrence 5, John Savage 3, S. Broadhurst 6, William Jones 1, J. E. Broadhurst 3, Isaac Wilson 1, Joseph Lowe 5, Henry McMahon 4, Wm. Butterworth 1, Henry Ricnardson 4, Harold Guest 3, Joseph Daintith 3, F. Clare 3, James Lawton 3, Stanley Hinde 5, Isaac Makin 2, Simeon Monks 5, Free Inca 4, Herbert. J. Hopkins 4, William E. Clare 3, T. A. Taylor 3, W. Challoner 4, Robert Dandy 3, J. H. Hurst 4, Samuel Wray 3, J. Riley 4.</p>
