      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-07-26_WidnesExaminer_art0220" n="art0220">
        <p>THE " BEWSEY CIRC</p>
        <p>The inhabitants of the Bewsey and Gorsey- lane districts can now enjoy the luxury of a ride in their own motor. It is not the type of car which denotes the possession of wealth on the part of the fortunate occupants, in fast those who ride in it claim their right to do so by the payment of the humble penny. In other wards, the motor 'bus service estab - lished by the Corporation for the conveni- ence of two populous but hitherto somewhat isolated districts, is now in full swing and is daily proving a much-appreciated boon. If public patronage continues at the present rate, there is every ground for believing that the service will prove a profitable one to the Corporation, but it remains to be seen whether traffic will show any appreciable decrease when the novelty of the new method of locomotion has worn off. At present there is a great deal of " joy-riding " on the Bewsey circulai route, quite a large number of passengers making the complete round merely for the pleasure and exhilaration of the experience. This form of amusement is highly popular with the children and it is good at times to see the 'bus laden with a score or more of smiling, cheering youngsters who consider the ride well worth the halfpenny which is costs them. -Up to this week, only one 'but has been available for each route, but a third vehicle has now arrived and will be kept as a</p>
