        <p>(Applause.) He was a man who spoke out, without fear or favour, and a strong and keen political fighter. (Applause.) Mr. LONGLASD seconded. He said no one had the cause of progress more deeply at heart than Councillor Roberts, and if he could do anything to further it he was willing to do so, even if it involved some sacrifice. (Applause.) The vote was accorded with cheers. , On the proposition of the CHAIRMAN, seconded by Mr. BICKERTON, a vote of thanks was passed to the com- mittee and Captain H. G. Roberts responded. RESULTS OF THE SPORTS. Great interest was taken in the sports, the events resulting as follows : Ladies' Potato Race : 1, Mrs. H. Sherburn ; 2, Mrs. P. Vernon. Ladies' Needle Threading Race: 1, Miss Massey ;2, Miss Thomson. Jockey Race : 1, Mr. A. S. Percival; 2, Mr. H. Kay, jun. Slow Bicycle : 1, Mr. A. Aston ; 2, Mr. C. Weir. Sack Race: 1, Mr. A. Atrial! ; 2, Mr. Higham. Boys' Flat Race : 1, J. Kay ;2, H. Kay, jun. Three-legged Race: 1, Messrs. Higham and Jones. Tug-of-War: 1, Whitley team; 2, Crosfleld's band team. THE WORKERS. It would be impossible to speak too highly of the splendid efforts of the workers who had had the arrangements in hand. The committee consisted of : Chairman, Captain H. G. Roberts, J.P., Messrs. W. H. Braysttaw' G. Taylor, R. Billington, A. Albinson, I. Lawton, .1. Rose, F. Hindley, F. Fox, H. Lightfoot, J. Roughsedge' R' . Turner F. Burrows, J. Fairhurst, H. Kay, W. H. Grounds. Judges, Messrs. C. Jackson Holmes, J.P., J. A. Ransoms, J. E. Birtles. Starter,slr. W. 11. Brayshaw. Clerks of course, Messrs. R. Turner, F. Borrows' G. Taylor. Marksmen. Messrs. W. H. Grounds, H. Kay. Competitors' stewards, Messrs. J. Rose, W. Warren. Hon. treasurer, Mr. W. H. Grounds; and hon. secretary to fete, Mr. S.Albinson.</p>
