        <p>BIRTHS, MARRIAGES, DEATHS. Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in the " Examiner " at the following rates:—Not exceeding 20 words Is. 6d. each every additional seven words, 6d. Marriages. FORSTER—EMERY.—On the 19th inst. at the Parish Church, by the Rev. Canon Willis, Joseph Forster to Sarah Ann Emery. GREENE—BIBBY.—On the 22nd inst., at St. Paul's, by the Rev. W. 13racecarnp, William Greene, B.A.' son of John Greene, of 22, Crosfield-street,to Janet Bibby, daughter of William Bibby, of 13, Arpley-street. LONGSHAW—OGDEN.—On the 22nd inst., at Gol borne-street Baptist Church. Warrington, by the Rev. George Curtis, Hill Cliffe, Mr. Thomas Longshaw, son of the late Mr. Samuel Longshaw, of Warrington to Miss Lily Ogden, daughter of the late Mr. Edward Ogden, of Todmorden.</p>
        <p>Deaths. ECKERSLEY.—On the 24th inst., at 38, Padgate-lane, Patience Eckersley, aged 75 years. No flowers by request. "May she rest in peace." SMITH.—On the 24th inst., at 284, Lovely-lane, Sarah Ann Smith, aged 54 yeare.</p>
